    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f0342acab4c5adc8c1c891151d430f70dabb295f49a31e224afbb3f51e0fc49f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Proof-grade scale is governed by coupled choices about certified representation, requested output, algorithm, sampling density, and arithmetic. Ball enclosures reduce storage and improve cache friendliness, count-only output avoids unnecessary localization, FFT methods reduce algorithmic work, and rigorous multiprecision plus denser sampling impose throughput costs; semantic sufficiency therefore recovers resources without discarding the enclosure and completeness obligations needed by the result.",
